{"summary":"This pull request introduces a ProfileHeader component that synchronizes derived state in an effect instead of calculating it directly during render.","rating":"needs-improvement","readiness":"changes-required","strengths":[],"assumptions":["The component is intended to display the combined first and last name derived directly from props."],"findings":[{"file":"src/features/profile/ProfileHeader.tsx","line":6,"endLine":10,"evidence":"  const [fullName, setFullName] = useState("");","title":"Derived state stored in useEffect and useState","why":"Storing derived values in state and updating them via useEffect causes an extra render pass on every prop change and adds unnecessary complexity.","fix":"Calculate the full name directly during render without state or effects.","suggestedCode":"export function ProfileHeader({ firstName, lastName }: Props) {
  const fullName = `${firstName} ${lastName}`;
